<article class="env-lemma" id="08EB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08EB">Lemma <span data-tag="08EB">36.10.7</span>.</a> Let $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ be an affine scheme. Let $M^\bullet $ be a complex of $A$-modules and let $E$ be the corresponding object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. Then $E$ is a perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ if and only if $M^\bullet $ is perfect as an object of $D(A)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a logical consequence of Lemmas <a href="/tag/08E7" data-tag="08E7">36.10.2</a> and <a href="/tag/08E9" data-tag="08E9">36.10.4</a>, Cohomology, Lemma <a href="/tag/08CQ" data-tag="08CQ">20.49.5</a>, and More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0658" data-tag="0658">15.76.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>